TI  - Pleural procedures and patient safety: a national BTS audit of practice.
PG  - 189-91
LID - 10.1136/thoraxjnl-2013-204812 [doi]
AB  - The BTS pleural procedures audit collected data over a 2-month period in June and 
      July 2011. In contrast with the 2010 audit, which focussed simply on chest drain 
      insertions, data on all pleural aspirations and local anaesthetic thoracoscopy 
      (LAT) was also collected. Ninety hospitals submitted data, covering a patient 
      population of 33 million. Twenty-one per cent of centres ran a specialist pleural 
      disease clinic, 71% had a nominated chest drain safety lead, and 20% had thoracic 
      surgery on site. Additionally, one-third of centres had a physician-led LAT 
      service.
